The audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants for a Michigan operator's license, reading at a plain-English level, plus newcomers and parents of teen drivers who use the same handbook. This section covers distracted driving and the hand-held phone ban, the general cell phone law with its emergency and hands-free exceptions, Kelsey's Law for teens with a Level One or Level Two license, seat belt requirements, and child safety seat and booster rules. It teaches which phone uses are banned and which are allowed, how teen phone rules differ by license level, who must buckle up, and how children must be restrained and seated. It assumes no prior driving knowledge and no prerequisites beyond literacy, so wording stays concrete, procedural and free of legal jargon throughout.
